,title,link,text,language,family
0,Makhuwa-Meetto | Accent Network,https://accentnetwork.com/makhuwa-meetto/,"Makhuwa-Meetto, spoken by around 3 million people in Mozambique, is part of the Bantu family within the Niger-Congo language group. It is widely used in daily life and cultural practices.",Makhuwa-Meetto,Niger-Congo
1,Makhuwa-Meetto in Mayotte people group profile | Joshua Project,https://joshuaproject.net/index.php/people_groups/13236/MF,"The Makhuwa-Meetto speak a language that is part of the Niger-Congo language family. They live in Tanzania, Mozambique and various islands off the coast of East Africa including the Comoros and Mayotte.",Makhuwa-Meetto,Niger-Congo
2,Makhuwa-Meetto - mgh (Niger-Congo) - PeopleGroups.org,https://peoplegroups.org/language/mgh/,"People Groups who primarily speak Makhuwa-Meetto. To download a comprehensive people group list in spreadsheet form, visit our Research Data page. Visualize lostness with powerful maps.",Makhuwa-Meetto,Niger-Congo
3,Makhuwa-Meetto – TIPs,https://tips.translation.bible/tip_language/mgh/,Niger-Congo > Atlantic-Congo > Volta-Congo > ...The following are two poetic translations of Psalm 3:1-3 produced in a workshop for translating the psalms so that they can be performed musically. The first translation is in Meetto and the second in Kom.,Makhuwa-Meetto,Niger-Congo
4,Makhuwa-Meetto Meaning - YouTube,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=l7125ue7iOE,Video shows what Makhuwa-Meetto means. A Bantu language spoken by more than one million people in Mozambique and Tanzania.. Makhuwa-Meetto Meaning.,Makhuwa-Meetto,Niger-Congo
5,Makhuwa language — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/Makhuwa_language,"Makhuwa, also known as Emakhuwa or Makua, is a Bantu language belonging to the Niger-Congo family, specifically within the P.30 Makua-Lomwe group, and is the most widely spoken indigenous language in Mozambique.",Makhuwa-Meetto,Niger-Congo
6,Makhuwa-Meetto Translator | Free & AI-Powered,https://anythingtranslate.com/translators/makhuwa-meetto-translator/,"Makhuwa-Meetto is a Bantu language primarily spoken in northern Mozambique. This tool seamlessly converts your text from any language into fluent Makhuwa-Meetto, bridging communication gaps and fostering deeper connections with this vibrant culture.",Makhuwa-Meetto,Niger-Congo
7,Makhuwa language,https://bliptext.com/articles/makhuwa-language,"Central Makhuwa (""Makhuwa-Makhuwana"") is the basis of the standard language. Ethnologue lists Central Makhuwa, Meetto–Ruvuma, Marrevone–Enahara, and Esaka as separate languages, and Chirima as six languages. The population figures are from Ethnologue for 2006.",Makhuwa-Meetto,Niger-Congo
8,Category:Makhuwa-Meetto terms derived from Niger-Congo...,https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Category:Makhuwa-Meetto_terms_derived_from_Niger-Congo_languages,"» Niger-Congo. Makhuwa-Meetto terms that originate from one of the Niger-Congo languages. This category should, ideally, contain only other categories. Entries can be categorized here, too, when the proper subcategory is unclear.",Makhuwa-Meetto,Niger-Congo
9,Glottolog 5.3 - Makhuwa-Meetto,https://glottolog.org/resource/languoid/id/makh1261,Leetugal Niger Fulfulde. Wodaabe.David M. Eberhard and Gary F. Simons and Charles D. Fennig 2025. Comment: Makhuwa-Meetto (mgh-mgh) = 5* (Developing). Glottocode: makh1261. ISO 639-3: mgh.,Makhuwa-Meetto,Niger-Congo
